## Animates/animators-sorveglianti school canteen and 1 animator/animator-sorvegliante additional school canteen

City of Locarno — public competition in Locarno (TI), Switzerland.

Bastian Lerch BL/cz 17 July 2026 ADVISO DI CONCORSO IL MUNICIPIO DI LOCARNO makes it known that the competition for the indefinite assignment of: 6 animators/animators-sorve school canteens and 1 animator/animator-surveying school canteen at our school canteen offices for students and pupils of the elementary school. The function of animator-sorvegliante can provide surveillance and service such as the accompaniment of students from/to the school office. The commitment focuses on four working days (Monday, Tuesday, Thursday and Friday) in the hourly period between 11:30 and 13:30 and coincides with the school calendar. The same conditions apply to the additional position. The person in charge will be employed mainly at the school canteen of Solduno (locali dell'Istituto San Carlo) and, if necessary, can be called to serve also at the other school canteens. Some positions are already occupied by staff in charge. Required Requirements
• proven experience in the field of childhood with groups of children (summer colonies, afterschool animators, extra-school activities, day families, Scout camps, Youth and Sport,...);
• ease of work in contact with school children (6-11) and strong relational skills.
• excellent knowledge of the Italian language (understanding and spoken at level C2 or above)
• sense of responsibility, reliability and guidance to quality and attitude to work both independent and in group
• organizational capacity, flexibility and spirit of initiative in respect of the educational continuity of teachers
• availability to participate in a specific compulsory training organized by the College of Inspectors of Municipal Schools. The entry into service is scheduled from Monday 31 August 2026. Remuneration The position is framed in the role of auxiliary/school institutes class 2 (according to the Organic Regulation of Collaborators and Locarno Collaborators). The expected salary fork, for 100% use, starts from CHF 45'405.- up to a maximum of 68'108.-, to which allowances for children must be added (CHF 2'580.- /CHF 3'216.-). This notice of competition is also visible on the website of the City at the following address www.locarno.ch/it/albo- comune/assunzioni-personale. The City Hall may not, in any case, consider applications and attachments transmitted through other channels (paper, email, fax, etc.) or incomplete applications. Applications must be submitted exclusively through the online portal by Monday 3 August 2026 at 23:59 2 accompanied by the following documents:
• curriculum vitae and motivation letter;
• certificates of study and work;
• medical certificate or self-certification downloadable on www.locarno.ch - virtual door section - different forms;
• copy identity document;
• copy work permit for persons of foreign nationality;
• photo passport size. The extract of the judicial box and the certificate of the Office of executions and bankruptcies will be required when convening the selection interview. Any further information may be requested directly by the Vice-Director of School Institutions, Mrs Tamara De Albuquerque at 091 756 34 27 or by e-mail at dealbuquerque.tamara@locarno.ch.

Sector:* Public Administration

Sede: Piazza Grande 18, 6600 Locarno, TI, Switzerland

